# Frontend Stack — read @design-rules.md before any frontend work

This project's frontend is **server-rendered Django templates + HTMX + Alpine.js
+ plain CSS**. There is no build step and no client-side framework.

**Before generating or editing any template, component, or frontend asset, read
[design-rules.md](mdc:design-rules.md) and follow it.** The full conventions
(HTMX partial patterns, Alpine scope, CSS tokens, template structure) live there.

## Hard constraints (never violate without asking first)

- **No React / Vue / Svelte / Next / any SPA framework** — not even for one
  component.
- **No JS build step** — no Vite, Webpack, esbuild, bundlers, `npm run build`
  for frontend. No JSX/TSX.
- **No Tailwind unless already configured** — use semantic CSS with `:root`
  custom-property tokens. Never hardcode hex values; add a token instead.
- **No JSON-rendered-to-DOM.** HTMX views return **HTML fragments**, not JSON.
  The server renders; the client swaps.
- **No heavy animation libs** (Framer Motion, GSAP). Motion is CSS
  (`transform`/`opacity` + `@keyframes`), gated on `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Server owns truth.** Real data comes from Django context or an HTMX
  fragment — never hardcoded in JS or held as authoritative state in Alpine.

## Defaults

- Reach for the smallest tool that works: **static HTML → HTMX → Alpine**.
- HTMX partials live in `templates/**/partials/` as `_name.html`; always include
  `{% csrf_token %}` in forms and give every swap a loading + error state.
- Alpine is for **local, ephemeral** UI state only (toggles, tabs, count-ups).
- Style only via `var(--token)`; every layout must survive a 380px viewport.

If a request seems to require anything on the banned list, **stop and explain
why in-stack won't work** before proposing an alternative — do not switch
silently.

## Mandatory: re-read the rules on EVERY design task

Before writing or editing **any** template, component, HTMX view, Alpine widget,
or CSS, you must **re-open and re-read [design-rules.md](mdc:design-rules.md)
first** — every time, not just the first task in a session. Context from an
earlier task is not a substitute for re-reading; rules drift out of attention
across a long session, which is exactly when violations happen.

**Start every frontend response by confirming compliance out loud**, in this
form, before any code:

```
Design-rules check:
- Stack: [what you're using — HTML/HTMX/Alpine/CSS] ✓
- Tokens: [using var(--…), no hardcoded hex] ✓
- Server-owns-truth: [data source is Django context / HTMX fragment] ✓
- Motion: [CSS only, reduced-motion gated — or N/A] ✓
- Swap states: [loading + error present — or N/A] ✓
```

If any line would be a ✗, stop and resolve it (or ask) before writing code. A
task that produces code without this check at the top is incomplete and should
be redone.
